   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun -e 'import {LoopDetector} from \"./src/harness/types.ts\"; const d=new LoopDetector(100); for(let i=0;i<5;i++){d.observe(\"shell\",\"poll\",String(i));d.observeResult(String(i),\"waiting\");} console.log(d.observe(\"shell\",\"poll\",\"5\")); d.observeResult(\"5\",\"progress\");'",
    "output": "repeated the same shell call 6 times"
   },
   "evidence": "HEAD immediately counts the new call with `this.recent.push({ key, call: this.total })` and returns a stop reason when `same >= this.maxIdenticalInWindow`, before its result arrives. Both harnesses then assign `stuckReason` and call `stuckController.abort()`; the later `observeResult` callback cannot retract that decision. Base also stopped immediately at invocation time, but the request explicitly requires a changed result to prevent that call from counting, making this an unfulfilled requirement."
